Changes in v6:
- this patch now also carries the live ethtool -L rx wiring
  (set_channels -> resize_rx_channels), the !opened down-path gate,
  desired_dma_for_rxqs() and drain_rx_queue(); P15 completes the
  down-path rollback and the mq_fallback max_rx cap
- harvest no_buffer counters before freeing buffer lists, and under
  the retiring queue's replenish_lock: netpoll reaches those queues
  until the surviving count is published and folds the same counters
  under that lock
- publish num_rx_queues before synchronize_net() so poll loops exit
  cleanly during scale-down
- use restart_rx_queue() rather than kick_rx_queue_if_pending() after the
  checked enable_irq() on scale-up and on the scale-down rollback, as
  suggested: kick cannot retry a queue whose replenish posted nothing,
  and the explicit rc check above both sites is untouched by the swap.
  That leaves kick with no callers, so drop it
- downgrade the range check in schedule_rx_queue() to a quiet return
  when only the upper bound trips: netpoll walks a snapshot of the
  queue count, so an ethtool -L rx shrink races it into a WARN that
  userspace can trigger at will. replenish_task() already skips the
  same race quietly, and callers read false as "queue is gone"
- drop leftover spin_lock_init() from alloc_single_rx_queue(); it runs
  on a live adapter during scale-up, so re-initialising the lock could
  race a netpoll replenish holding it. probe owns lock init
- zero buffer_list_dma[] on the alloc_single_rx_queue() map-failure
  path rather than leaving DMA_MAPPING_ERROR in it; the bulk
  allocator already does this and free_single_rx_queue() keys its
  unmap on that field
- do not add a !multi_queue gate above the no-op check; the single
  gate below it already rejects rx > 1, and the duplicate had to be
  deleted again in P15
- comment why that gate refuses any rx > 1 rather than only growth:
  under mq_fallback the next open comes up single-queue, so an
  intermediate count would be clamped there anyway, and max_rx stays
  at the live count only to keep TX-only ethtool -L working
- correct the survivor-restart comment: the teardown loops walk
  new_count..old_count-1, so a shrink never stops a survivor. The
  restart stays as cheap insurance for a queue left masked by the poll
  tail's enable_irq() failure exit, not as shrink cleanup
- commit message: state the scale-up order as the code has it
  (publish, replenish, napi_enable, then PHYP unmask), and note the
  transient RPS WARN while real_num_rx_queues trails the live count
- commit message: say why deregistration precedes the pool unmap, that
  PHYP has to release buffer ownership while the metadata its
  correlators index is still valid. This is the ordering rationale
  only; the v5 text also called it a hang root cause, which stays out
  since the parent has no resize path to have hung
- commit message: restore the -EINVAL guard on the RX range, which P15
  documents for the mirror-image TX case

